{{!
    Shared page header: one muted line of context and the way back to the
    dashboard.

    The title of the page is NOT here. Moodle prints the page heading itself,
    as the one top level heading of the document, and a second one inside the
    content would repeat it and leave two h1 on the page. Every page of this
    plugin therefore sets its own $PAGE heading, and this partial only carries
    what the theme cannot know: the scanned versions, the verdict, the score
    and the button.

    The results table and the scan history both start with this partial, so
    the two pages cannot drift apart in badges, buttons or spacing. The
    matching rules live in styles.css under .upgradeguard-pagehead.

    Context:
    * backurl: where the secondary button goes.
    * currentversion, targetversion: optional, the scanned pair (results page).
    * verdict, verdictclass: optional badge with the verdict of the scan.
    * score, hasscore: optional readiness score of the scan.
    * meta: optional plain text line, for example the number of recorded scans.
}}
<div class="upgradeguard-pagehead d-flex justify-content-between align-items-start">
    <p class="upgradeguard-pagehead-meta text-muted mb-0">
        {{#currentversion}}<span>{{currentversion}} &rarr; {{targetversion}}</span>{{/currentversion}}
        {{#meta}}<span>{{meta}}</span>{{/meta}}
        {{#verdict}}<span class="badge upgradeguard-verdict upgradeguard-verdict-{{verdictclass}}">{{verdict}}</span>{{/verdict}}
        {{#hasscore}}<span class="upgradeguard-pagehead-score upgradeguard-score upgradeguard-score-{{verdictclass}}">{{score}}</span>{{/hasscore}}
    </p>
    {{#backurl}}
    <a class="btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm" href="{{backurl}}">{{#str}}backtodashboard, tool_upgradeguard{{/str}}</a>
    {{/backurl}}
</div>
